 },
 {
  "id": "a6c903d4-5a89-4145-b8ef-bcc298e6ec99",
  "type": "heading",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left",
   "level": 2,
   "isToggleable": false
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Two documents, not one",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "f48185e5-f9fc-43a1-ab1f-bdb3b2def8fd",
  "type": "paragraph",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Markdown is what a note ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "says",
    "styles": {
     "bold": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": ". The outline is what it is ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "made of",
    "styles": {
     "bold": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " — one line per block, id first:",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "c1235732-67ad-4936-85f8-83c51d6e4bc7",
  "type": "codeBlock",
  "props": {
   "language": "text"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "95070957-a96a-4bbe-87cc-eac08c08e168  heading  Rate limits\n28cfe6fd-f9df-4774-aae4-11528a391c76  paragraph  Sixty a minute, per token, counted in Redis.\n2505db4c-3046-4d44-a3a6-c1a7b3a0d581  bulletListItem  429 carries Retry-After, in seconds.",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "77dc1d58-69d0-4bef-b6a7-9c80091b6ad3",
  "type": "paragraph",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Reading a whole note to change one paragraph is what this is built to make unnecessary: read the outline, then name the block.",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "71b23eb8-a89f-4087-8456-0b375674c6cf",
  "type": "codeBlock",
  "props": {
   "language": "json"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "{\n  \"note\": \"Tour/4. Notes an agent can edit.note\",\n  \"ops\": [\n    { \"op\": \"replace\", \"id\": \"<the id from the outline>\", \"markdown\": \"Ninety a minute now.\" },\n    { \"op\": \"after\",   \"id\": \"<the id from the outline>\", \"markdown\": \"- `429` is not retried automatically.\" }\n  ]\n}",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "e5d41d1c-d98d-4881-83f7-40c577f7fed4",
  "type": "paragraph",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "And ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "a block nobody edited keeps its id",
    "styles": {
     "bold": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": ", because the editor holds the caret, the undo stack and the selection by block id. A write that mints fresh ids for a note somebody has open is a note that jumps under them.",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "ed739ded-2718-4e62-8bc2-1607376ff393",
  "type": "heading",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left",
   "level": 2,
   "isToggleable": false
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "What it refuses, and why",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "abfa5ead-56bb-443f-848d-a37841182b86",
  "type": "bulletListItem",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "`write_note` argues before it rewrites.",
    "styles": {
     "bold": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " Colours, alignment, underline, merged cells and column widths have no markdown syntax, so it names the ones this note would lose and asks for ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "force",
    "styles": {
     "code": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " if you meant it. ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "edit_note",
    "styles": {
     "code": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " never has to ask — it only touches the blocks you named.",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "32bbb8b7-559c-43d7-b78b-9b34e500a6a4",
  "type": "bulletListItem",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "A block markdown cannot express is carried, not dropped.",
    "styles": {
     "bold": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " A drawing, a video, an audio clip, an attachment or a block from a later version of the editor each becomes an HTML comment holding the block itself: invisible where markdown is rendered, exact on the way back. Deleting one is then a decision rather than an accident.",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "a1e7ced2-3cc8-4d1a-8fba-8fe4c8b8b54e",
  "type": "bulletListItem",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "It will not introduce a block this editor cannot open.",
    "styles": {
     "bold": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " A type the note already had is carried, because refusing that would make such a note unfixable. See ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "spec.note",
    "styles": {
     "code": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": ".",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "86781fe8-e9c0-4510-af2c-e86f3c723120",
  "type": "heading",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left",
   "level": 2,
   "isToggleable": false
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "The one thing it cannot see",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "46b185f9-d555-41aa-8f43-5b3cea7de712",
  "type": "quote",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "VS Code writes nothing to disk until you save, and will not reload a document with unsaved changes. So a write into a note that is open and ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "dirty",
    "styles": {
     "bold": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " is a write the next ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "⌘S",
    "styles": {
     "code": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " silently undoes — and nothing outside the editor can find that out. Every tool that writes says so in its own description.",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "b1a8b6a1-53a7-4387-80ec-d357bf0f9429",
  "type": "paragraph",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "The studio does not have this problem: it reads the open document's text and writes through a workspace edit. Closing it properly for the server means the same move, and that is the next program to write rather than a setting to find.",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "328e915f-dc71-4c22-a8aa-c7bd33e8a255",
  "type": "heading",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left",
   "level": 2,
   "isToggleable": false
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Try it",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "798239d9-07ce-41cb-8395-970d38e29201",
  "type": "numberedListItem",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Ask for a summary: “read the notes in ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "sample/Tour",
    "styles": {
     "code": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " and tell me what this extension is”.",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "13bf1345-ecb6-48fe-9106-25190f5c0478",
  "type": "numberedListItem",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Ask for an edit: “add a ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Seen also",
    "styles": {
     "bold": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " heading to the end of ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Welcome.note",
    "styles": {
     "code": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " listing the tour notes”.",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "a8347272-649c-472b-9961-00f11f697cc5",
  "type": "numberedListItem",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Ask for the cheap read: “show me the outline of ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "spec.note",
    "styles": {
     "code": true
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": " and say which blocks are folded”.",
    "styles": {}
   }
  ],
  "children": []
 },
 {
  "id": "b04dd625-8656-4b56-a736-5cf2e63ef013",
  "type": "numberedListItem",
  "props": {
   "backgroundColor": "default",
   "textColor": "default",
   "textAlignment": "left"
  },
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "text",
    "text": "Then save the file yourself and watch ",
    "styles": {}
   },
   {
